url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/versions-cleaner/commits/c82adbf3ba68829f25b04fbe40c9726da4b51604"}],"sha":"a213b8a141a6370300f4d491953e1ddfba9380dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/versions-cleaner/commits/a213b8a141a6370300f4d491953e1ddfba9380dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/versions-cleaner/commits/c82adbf3ba68829f25b04fbe40c9726da4b51604/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T05:52:44Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T05:52:44Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSE"},"message":"fix: harden destructive version-retention logic and config guards\n\nBehavior-preserving safety hardening of the JCR version-deletion paths.\n\nS1 (CleanCommand.keepLastNVersions / retainNewestVersions): extract the\n  retention trim into a clamped helper. The previous\n  subList(size - nbToKeep, size) could compute a negative fromIndex when the\n  guard count (nbVersions, which varies by useVersioningApi/versionLabels)\n  diverged from the materialised non-root list size, throwing\n  IndexOutOfBoundsException that was silently swallowed. Cut point now clamped\n  to [0, size]; normal-path deletion counts unchanged.\nR1: unit-tested retention bounds (keep 0/N/exact/over-size/empty).\n\nS2 (CleanCommand): replace broad catch logging at info with error + version\n  history path context. Per-history failure is still isolated so the scan\n  continues, but a failed destructive operation is now visible.\n\nS3 (CleanerContext.refreshSessions): guard non-positive sessionRefreshInterval\n  (modulo-by-zero ArithmeticException would abort the scan mid-batch) and\n  null-check sessions before refresh.\nR3: unit-tested zero/negative interval and null-session tolerance.\n\nS4 (CleanCommand.getNode): extract parent/self traversal validation into pure,\n  package-private normalizeSubtreePath so the version-storage-escape guard is\n  unit-testable; getNode behavior unchanged.\nR4: unit-tested leading-slash strip and ../. rejection.\n\nS5: magic numbers to named constants — ROOT_VERSION_COUNT,\n  MAX_PRINTABLE_NAME_LENGTH (CleanCommand); DEFAULT_SESSION_REFRESH_INTERVAL,\n  DEFAULT_LONG_HISTORY_PURGE_THRESHOLD (CleanerContext).\n\nAdds JUnit4/AssertJ/Mockito test-scoped deps (repo had 0 tests). 18 tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"d9d66805d59c4c1e62e8ee49e3007c373490f5f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/versions-cleaner/git/trees/d9d66805d59c4c1e62e8ee49e3007c373490f5f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/versions-cleaner/git/commits/c82adbf3ba68829f25b04fbe40c9726da4b51604","verification":{"payload":"tree d9d66805d59c4c1e62e8ee49e3007c373490f5f0\nparent 7e277f71820238645d46993b06d4df1c58adabdb\nauthor Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781070764 +0200\ncommitter Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781070764 +0200\n\nfix: harden destructive version-retention logic and config guards\n\nBehavior-preserving safety hardening of the JCR version-deletion paths.\n\nS1 (CleanCommand.keepLastNVersions / retainNewestVersions): extract the\n  retention trim into a clamped helper. The previous\n  subList(size - nbToKeep, size) could compute a negative fromIndex when the\n  guard count (nbVersions, which varies by useVersioningApi/versionLabels)\n  diverged from the materialised non-root list size, throwing\n  IndexOutOfBoundsException that was silently swallowed. Cut point now clamped\n  to [0, size]; normal-path deletion counts unchanged.\nR1: unit-tested retention bounds (keep 0/N/exact/over-size/empty).\n\nS2 (CleanCommand): replace broad catch logging at info with error + version\n  history path context. Per-history failure is still isolated so the scan\n  continues, but a failed destructive operation is now visible.\n\nS3 (CleanerContext.refreshSessions): guard non-positive sessionRefreshInterval\n  (modulo-by-zero ArithmeticException would abort the scan mid-batch) and\n  null-check sessions before refresh.\nR3: unit-tested zero/negative interval and null-session tolerance.\n\nS4 (CleanCommand.getNode): extract parent/self traversal validation into pure,\n  package-private normalizeSubtreePath so the version-storage-escape guard is\n  unit-testable; getNode behavior unchanged.\nR4: unit-tested leading-slash strip and ../. rejection.\n\nS5: magic numbers to named constants — ROOT_VERSION_COUNT,\n  MAX_PRINTABLE_NAME_LENGTH (CleanCommand); DEFAULT_SESSION_REFRESH_INTERVAL,\n  DEFAULT_LONG_HISTORY_PURGE_THRESHOLD (CleanerContext).\n\nAdds JUnit4/AssertJ/Mockito test-scoped deps (repo had 0 tests). 18 tests pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQEzBAABCgAdFiEEtcDrrZ6KblczSEt9UhsGUDwSL3kFAmoo+6wACgkQUhsGUDwS\nL3n+pAgAhpo7C80uwPZ4BWNiLSSbWd/XAfroDWF5jmLYvmjsiB3fOQLhYsfcWEtG\nVGka+N11QA6oWUD5cNgfT6mnYUDZwSrOC6abcuoXwvWvdJjiph71LZ08D5FenhmJ\nc6GoBkSNYtbXckzXrJxVZPOA9b9RyqDv5BWiwJr2GnEgNFhrprnFxuR